Q4. Will this compile?

interface Calculator {
    int calculate(int a, int b);
}

Calculator c = (a, b) -> {
    System.out.println(a + b);
};

ANSWER:
NO — Compile-time error.

Reason:
calculate() returns int, but the lambda does not return anything.

Correct:

Calculator c = (a, b) -> {
    System.out.println(a + b);
    return a + b;
};


