Q11. Predict the output.

int x = 10;

interface A {
    void show();
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int x = 20;

        A a = () -> System.out.println(x);

        a.show();
    }
}

ANSWER:
20

Reason:
The lambda captures the local variable x from main().


------------------------------------------------------------

Q12. Will this compile?

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int x = 10;

        Runnable r = () -> {
            x++;
            System.out.println(x);
        };

        r.run();
    }
}

ANSWER:
NO — Compile-time error.

Reason:
A local variable captured by a lambda must be
final or effectively final.

x++;

modifies x, so x is NOT effectively final.


